cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite the research draft in preferred-citation below and identify the
  repository version used. This file describes release v0.1.0.
title: "Degree-3 spectral refinement research and verification package"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-06"
repository-code: "https://github.com/swihart/minvol-degree3-spectral-bound"
url: "https://github.com/swihart/minvol-degree3-spectral-bound/releases/tag/v0.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Swihart"
    given-names: "Bruce J."
abstract: >-
  Reproducible research package for an AI-assisted degree-3 spectral
  refinement of Nishioka's lower bound for the three-dimensional
  Blaschke-Lebesgue problem. The package contains a LaTeX manuscript, expanded
  proof notes, exact symbolic Python checks, independent R tests, and automated
  build and preflight workflows. The result is a non-peer-reviewed research
  draft seeking independent mathematical verification.
keywords:
  - "bodies of constant width"
  - "Blaschke-Lebesgue problem"
  - "spherical harmonics"
  - "convex geometry"
  - "reproducible research"
